---Details of an instance (also called a node interchangeably) in a SageMaker HyperPod cluster.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeDetails
---@field InstanceGroupName? aws.sagemaker.ClusterInstanceGroupName The instance group name in which the instance is.
---@field InstanceId? string The ID of the instance.
---@field NodeLogicalId? aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeLogicalId A unique identifier for the node that persists throughout its lifecycle, from provisioning request to termination. This identifier can be used to track the node even before it has an assigned InstanceId.
---@field InstanceStatus? aws.sagemaker.ClusterInstanceStatusDetails The status of the instance.
---@field InstanceType? aws.sagemaker.ClusterInstanceType The type of the instance.
---@field LaunchTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp The time when the instance is launched.
---@field LastSoftwareUpdateTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp The time when the cluster was last updated.
---@field LifeCycleConfig? aws.sagemaker.ClusterLifeCycleConfig The LifeCycle configuration applied to the instance.
---@field OverrideVpcConfig? aws.sagemaker.VpcConfig The customized Amazon VPC configuration at the instance group level that overrides the default Amazon VPC configuration of the SageMaker HyperPod cluster.
---@field ThreadsPerCore? aws.sagemaker.ClusterThreadsPerCore The number of threads per CPU core you specified under CreateCluster.
---@field InstanceStorageConfigs? aws.sagemaker.ClusterInstanceStorageConfigs The configurations of additional storage specified to the instance group where the instance (node) is launched.
---@field PrivatePrimaryIp? aws.sagemaker.ClusterPrivatePrimaryIp The private primary IP address of the SageMaker HyperPod cluster node.
---@field PrivatePrimaryIpv6? aws.sagemaker.ClusterPrivatePrimaryIpv6 The private primary IPv6 address of the SageMaker HyperPod cluster node when configured with an Amazon VPC that supports IPv6 and includes subnets with IPv6 addressing enabled in either the cluster Amazon VPC configuration or the instance group Amazon VPC configuration.
---@field PrivateDnsHostname? aws.sagemaker.ClusterPrivateDnsHostname The private DNS hostname of the SageMaker HyperPod cluster node.
---@field Placement? aws.sagemaker.ClusterInstancePlacement The placement details of the SageMaker HyperPod cluster node.
---@field CurrentImageId? aws.sagemaker.ImageId The ID of the Amazon Machine Image (AMI) currently in use by the node.
---@field DesiredImageId? aws.sagemaker.ImageId The ID of the Amazon Machine Image (AMI) desired for the node.
---@field CurrentImageReleaseVersion? aws.sagemaker.ImageReleaseVersion The version of the HyperPod-managed AMI currently running on the node.
---@field DesiredImageReleaseVersion? aws.sagemaker.ImageReleaseVersion The desired version of the HyperPod-managed AMI for the node. This may differ from the current version when an update is pending.
---@field ImageVersionStatus? aws.sagemaker.ClusterImageVersionStatus The status of the image version for the cluster node.
---@field UltraServerInfo? aws.sagemaker.UltraServerInfo Contains information about the UltraServer.
---@field KubernetesConfig? aws.sagemaker.ClusterKubernetesConfigNodeDetails The Kubernetes configuration applied to this node, showing both the current and desired state of labels and taints. The cluster works to reconcile the actual state with the declared state.
---@field CapacityType? aws.sagemaker.ClusterCapacityType The capacity type of the node. Valid values are OnDemand and Spot. When set to OnDemand, the node is launched as an On-Demand instance. When set to Spot, the node is launched as a Spot instance.
---@field NetworkInterface? aws.sagemaker.ClusterNetworkInterfaceDetails The network interface configuration for the cluster node.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeId string

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeIds aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeId[]

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeLogicalId string

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeLogicalIdList aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeLogicalId[]

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeProvisioningMode "Continuous"

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeRecovery "Automatic"|"None"

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeSummaries aws.sagemaker.ClusterNodeSummary[]

---Lists a summary of the properties of an instance (also called a node interchangeably) of a SageMaker HyperPod cluster.
