---@class aws.sagemaker.CreateModelPackageInput
---@field ModelPackageName? aws.sagemaker.EntityName The name of the model package. The name must have 1 to 63 characters. Valid characters are a-z, A-Z, 0-9, and - (hyphen).
---@field ModelPackageGroupName? aws.sagemaker.ArnOrName The name or Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the model package group that this model version belongs to.
---@field ModelPackageDescription? aws.sagemaker.EntityDescription A description of the model package.
---@field ModelPackageRegistrationType? aws.sagemaker.ModelPackageRegistrationType|string The package registration type of the model package input.
---@field InferenceSpecification? aws.sagemaker.InferenceSpecification Specifies details about inference jobs that you can run with models based on this model package, including the following information:
---@field ValidationSpecification? aws.sagemaker.ModelPackageValidationSpecification Specifies configurations for one or more transform jobs that SageMaker runs to test the model package.
---@field SourceAlgorithmSpecification? aws.sagemaker.SourceAlgorithmSpecification Details about the algorithm that was used to create the model package.
---@field CertifyForMarketplace? aws.sagemaker.CertifyForMarketplace Whether to certify the model package for listing on Amazon Web Services Marketplace.
---@field Tags? aws.sagemaker.TagList A list of key value pairs associated with the model. For more information, see Tagging Amazon Web Services resources in the Amazon Web Services General Reference Guide.
---@field ModelApprovalStatus? aws.sagemaker.ModelApprovalStatus|string Whether the model is approved for deployment.
---@field MetadataProperties? aws.sagemaker.MetadataProperties
---@field ModelMetrics? aws.sagemaker.ModelMetrics A structure that contains model metrics reports.
---@field ClientToken? aws.sagemaker.ClientToken A unique token that guarantees that the call to this API is idempotent.
---@field Domain? aws.sagemaker.String The machine learning domain of your model package and its components. Common machine learning domains include computer vision and natural language processing.
---@field Task? aws.sagemaker.String The machine learning task your model package accomplishes. Common machine learning tasks include object detection and image classification. The following tasks are supported by Inference Recommender: "IMAGE_CLASSIFICATION" | "OBJECT_DETECTION" | "TEXT_GENERATION" |"IMAGE_SEGMENTATION" | "FILL_MASK" | "CLASSIFICATION" | "REGRESSION" | "OTHER".
---@field SamplePayloadUrl? aws.sagemaker.S3Uri The Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) path where the sample payload is stored. This path must point to a single gzip compressed tar archive (.tar.gz suffix). This archive can hold multiple files that are all equally used in the load test. Each file in the archive must satisfy the size constraints of the InvokeEndpoint call.
---@field CustomerMetadataProperties? aws.sagemaker.CustomerMetadataMap The metadata properties associated with the model package versions.
---@field DriftCheckBaselines? aws.sagemaker.DriftCheckBaselines Represents the drift check baselines that can be used when the model monitor is set using the model package. For more information, see the topic on Drift Detection against Previous Baselines in SageMaker Pipelines in the Amazon SageMaker Developer Guide.
---@field AdditionalInferenceSpecifications? aws.sagemaker.AdditionalInferenceSpecifications An array of additional Inference Specification objects. Each additional Inference Specification specifies artifacts based on this model package that can be used on inference endpoints. Generally used with SageMaker Neo to store the compiled artifacts.
---@field SkipModelValidation? aws.sagemaker.SkipModelValidation|string Indicates if you want to skip model validation.
---@field SourceUri? aws.sagemaker.ModelPackageSourceUri The URI of the source for the model package. If you want to clone a model package, set it to the model package Amazon Resource Name (ARN). If you want to register a model, set it to the model ARN.
---@field SecurityConfig? aws.sagemaker.ModelPackageSecurityConfig The KMS Key ID (KMSKeyId) used for encryption of model package information.
---@field ModelCard? aws.sagemaker.ModelPackageModelCard The model card associated with the model package. Since ModelPackageModelCard is tied to a model package, it is a specific usage of a model card and its schema is simplified compared to the schema of ModelCard. The ModelPackageModelCard schema does not include model_package_details, and model_overview is composed of the model_creator and model_artifact properties. For more information about the mo...
---@field ModelLifeCycle? aws.sagemaker.ModelLifeCycle A structure describing the current state of the model in its life cycle.
---@field ManagedStorageType? aws.sagemaker.ManagedStorageType|string The storage type of the model package.

---@class aws.sagemaker.CreateModelPackageOutput
---@field ModelPackageArn aws.sagemaker.ModelPackageArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the new model package.

