---@class aws.sagemaker.DescribeTrainingJobRequest
---@field TrainingJobName aws.sagemaker.TrainingJobName The name of the training job.

---@class aws.sagemaker.DescribeTrainingJobResponse
---@field TrainingJobName aws.sagemaker.TrainingJobName Name of the model training job.
---@field TrainingJobArn aws.sagemaker.TrainingJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the training job.
---@field TuningJobArn? aws.sagemaker.HyperParameterTuningJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the associated hyperparameter tuning job if the training job was launched by a hyperparameter tuning job.
---@field LabelingJobArn? aws.sagemaker.LabelingJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the SageMaker Ground Truth labeling job that created the transform or training job.
---@field AutoMLJobArn? aws.sagemaker.AutoMLJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of an AutoML job.
---@field ModelArtifacts aws.sagemaker.ModelArtifacts Information about the Amazon S3 location that is configured for storing model artifacts.
---@field TrainingJobStatus aws.sagemaker.TrainingJobStatus The status of the training job.
---@field SecondaryStatus aws.sagemaker.SecondaryStatus Provides detailed information about the state of the training job. For detailed information on the secondary status of the training job, see StatusMessage under SecondaryStatusTransition.
---@field FailureReason? aws.sagemaker.FailureReason If the training job failed, the reason it failed.
---@field HyperParameters? aws.sagemaker.HyperParameters Algorithm-specific parameters.
---@field AlgorithmSpecification? aws.sagemaker.AlgorithmSpecification Information about the algorithm used for training, and algorithm metadata.
---@field RoleArn? aws.sagemaker.RoleArn The Amazon Web Services Identity and Access Management (IAM) role configured for the training job.
---@field InputDataConfig? aws.sagemaker.InputDataConfig An array of Channel objects that describes each data input channel.
---@field OutputDataConfig? aws.sagemaker.OutputDataConfig The S3 path where model artifacts that you configured when creating the job are stored. SageMaker creates subfolders for model artifacts.
---@field ResourceConfig? aws.sagemaker.ResourceConfig Resources, including ML compute instances and ML storage volumes, that are configured for model training.
---@field WarmPoolStatus? aws.sagemaker.WarmPoolStatus The status of the warm pool associated with the training job.
---@field VpcConfig? aws.sagemaker.VpcConfig A VpcConfig object that specifies the VPC that this training job has access to. For more information, see Protect Training Jobs by Using an Amazon Virtual Private Cloud.
---@field StoppingCondition aws.sagemaker.StoppingCondition Specifies a limit to how long a model training job can run. It also specifies how long a managed Spot training job has to complete. When the job reaches the time limit, SageMaker ends the training job. Use this API to cap model training costs.
---@field CreationTime aws.sagemaker.Timestamp A timestamp that indicates when the training job was created.
---@field TrainingStartTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp Indicates the time when the training job starts on training instances. You are billed for the time interval between this time and the value of TrainingEndTime. The start time in CloudWatch Logs might be later than this time. The difference is due to the time it takes to download the training data and to the size of the training container.
---@field TrainingEndTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp Indicates the time when the training job ends on training instances. You are billed for the time interval between the value of TrainingStartTime and this time. For successful jobs and stopped jobs, this is the time after model artifacts are uploaded. For failed jobs, this is the time when SageMaker detects a job failure.
---@field LastModifiedTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp A timestamp that indicates when the status of the training job was last modified.
---@field SecondaryStatusTransitions? aws.sagemaker.SecondaryStatusTransitions A history of all of the secondary statuses that the training job has transitioned through.
---@field FinalMetricDataList? aws.sagemaker.FinalMetricDataList A collection of MetricData objects that specify the names, values, and dates and times that the training algorithm emitted to Amazon CloudWatch.
---@field EnableNetworkIsolation? aws.sagemaker.Boolean If you want to allow inbound or outbound network calls, except for calls between peers within a training cluster for distributed training, choose True. If you enable network isolation for training jobs that are configured to use a VPC, SageMaker downloads and uploads customer data and model artifacts through the specified VPC, but the training container does not have network access.
---@field EnableInterContainerTrafficEncryption? aws.sagemaker.Boolean To encrypt all communications between ML compute instances in distributed training, choose True. Encryption provides greater security for distributed training, but training might take longer. How long it takes depends on the amount of communication between compute instances, especially if you use a deep learning algorithms in distributed training.
---@field EnableManagedSpotTraining? aws.sagemaker.Boolean A Boolean indicating whether managed spot training is enabled (True) or not (False).
---@field CheckpointConfig? aws.sagemaker.CheckpointConfig
---@field TrainingTimeInSeconds? aws.sagemaker.TrainingTimeInSeconds The training time in seconds.
---@field BillableTimeInSeconds? aws.sagemaker.BillableTimeInSeconds The billable time in seconds. Billable time refers to the absolute wall-clock time.
---@field BillableTokenCount? aws.sagemaker.BillableTokenCount The billable token count for eligible serverless training jobs.
---@field DebugHookConfig? aws.sagemaker.DebugHookConfig
---@field ExperimentConfig? aws.sagemaker.ExperimentConfig
---@field DebugRuleConfigurations? aws.sagemaker.DebugRuleConfigurations Configuration information for Amazon SageMaker Debugger rules for debugging output tensors.
---@field TensorBoardOutputConfig? aws.sagemaker.TensorBoardOutputConfig
---@field DebugRuleEvaluationStatuses? aws.sagemaker.DebugRuleEvaluationStatuses Evaluation status of Amazon SageMaker Debugger rules for debugging on a training job.
---@field ProfilerConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProfilerConfig
---@field ProfilerRuleConfigurations? aws.sagemaker.ProfilerRuleConfigurations Configuration information for Amazon SageMaker Debugger rules for profiling system and framework metrics.
---@field ProfilerRuleEvaluationStatuses? aws.sagemaker.ProfilerRuleEvaluationStatuses Evaluation status of Amazon SageMaker Debugger rules for profiling on a training job.
---@field ProfilingStatus? aws.sagemaker.ProfilingStatus Profiling status of a training job.
---@field Environment? aws.sagemaker.TrainingEnvironmentMap The environment variables to set in the Docker container.
---@field RetryStrategy? aws.sagemaker.RetryStrategy The number of times to retry the job when the job fails due to an InternalServerError.
---@field RemoteDebugConfig? aws.sagemaker.RemoteDebugConfig Configuration for remote debugging. To learn more about the remote debugging functionality of SageMaker, see Access a training container through Amazon Web Services Systems Manager (SSM) for remote debugging.
---@field InfraCheckConfig? aws.sagemaker.InfraCheckConfig Contains information about the infrastructure health check configuration for the training job.
---@field ServerlessJobConfig? aws.sagemaker.ServerlessJobConfig The configuration for serverless training jobs.
---@field MlflowConfig? aws.sagemaker.MlflowConfig The MLflow configuration using SageMaker managed MLflow.
---@field ModelPackageConfig? aws.sagemaker.ModelPackageConfig The configuration for the model package.
---@field MlflowDetails? aws.sagemaker.MlflowDetails The MLflow details of this job.
---@field ProgressInfo? aws.sagemaker.TrainingProgressInfo The Serverless training job progress information.
---@field OutputModelPackageArn? aws.sagemaker.ModelPackageArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the output model package containing model weights or checkpoints.

