---@field EnforcementMode aws.sagemaker.AvailabilityZoneBalanceEnforcementMode|string Determines how strictly the Availability Zone balance constraint is enforced.
---@field MaxImbalance? aws.sagemaker.AvailabilityZoneBalanceMaxImbalance The maximum allowed difference in the number of inference component copies between any two Availability Zones. This parameter applies only when the endpoint has instances across two or more Availability Zones. A copy placement is allowed if it reduces imbalance or the resulting imbalance is within this value.

---Specifies the type and size of the endpoint capacity to activate for a rolling deployment or a rollback strategy. You can specify your batches as either of the following:
---@class aws.sagemaker.InferenceComponentCapacitySize
---@field Type aws.sagemaker.InferenceComponentCapacitySizeType|string Specifies the endpoint capacity type.
---@field Value aws.sagemaker.CapacitySizeValue Defines the capacity size, either as a number of inference component copies or a capacity percentage.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.InferenceComponentCapacitySizeType "COPY_COUNT"|"CAPACITY_PERCENT"

---Defines the compute resources to allocate to run a model, plus any adapter models, that you assign to an inference component. These resources include CPU cores, accelerators, and memory.
---@class aws.sagemaker.InferenceComponentComputeResourceRequirements
---@field NumberOfCpuCoresRequired? aws.sagemaker.NumberOfCpuCores The number of CPU cores to allocate to run a model that you assign to an inference component.
---@field NumberOfAcceleratorDevicesRequired? aws.sagemaker.NumberOfAcceleratorDevices The number of accelerators to allocate to run a model that you assign to an inference component. Accelerators include GPUs and Amazon Web Services Inferentia.
---@field MinMemoryRequiredInMb aws.sagemaker.MemoryInMb The minimum MB of memory to allocate to run a model that you assign to an inference component.
---@field MaxMemoryRequiredInMb? aws.sagemaker.MemoryInMb The maximum MB of memory to allocate to run a model that you assign to an inference component.
---@field AcceleratorPartitionType? aws.sagemaker.AcceleratorPartitionType The accelerator partition profile this inference component occupies; on NVIDIA GPUs this is a Multi-Instance GPU (MIG) profile such as mig-3g.40gb. It must be one of the partition profiles declared in the target endpoint's accelerator partition layout, and when set, NumberOfAcceleratorDevicesRequired must be 1. This field is required when the endpoint's production variant has an accelerator partit...

---Defines a container that provides the runtime environment for a model that you deploy with an inference component.
---@class aws.sagemaker.InferenceComponentContainerSpecification
---@field Image? aws.sagemaker.ContainerImage The Amazon Elastic Container Registry (Amazon ECR) path where the Docker image for the model is stored.
---@field ArtifactUrl? aws.sagemaker.Url The Amazon S3 path where the model artifacts, which result from model training, are stored. This path must point to a single gzip compressed tar archive (.tar.gz suffix).
---@field Environment? aws.sagemaker.EnvironmentMap The environment variables to set in the Docker container. Each key and value in the Environment string-to-string map can have length of up to 1024. We support up to 16 entries in the map.
---@field ContainerMetricsConfig? aws.sagemaker.ContainerMetricsConfig The configuration for container metrics scraping. Specifies the metrics endpoint path and publishing frequency for the inference component's container. If not specified when EnableDetailedObservability is True, the default path /metrics on port 8080 is used. For first-party and Deep Learning Containers (DLC), the endpoint path is determined automatically and this configuration is optional.

---Details about the resources that are deployed with this inference component.
---@class aws.sagemaker.InferenceComponentContainerSpecificationSummary
---@field DeployedImage? aws.sagemaker.DeployedImage
---@field ArtifactUrl? aws.sagemaker.Url The Amazon S3 path where the model artifacts are stored.
---@field Environment? aws.sagemaker.EnvironmentMap The environment variables to set in the Docker container.
---@field ContainerMetricsConfig? aws.sagemaker.ContainerMetricsConfig The container metrics scraping configuration for this inference component, including the metrics endpoint path and publishing frequency.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.InferenceComponentCopyCount number

