---An Amazon SageMaker processing job that is used to analyze data and evaluate models. For more information, see Process Data and Evaluate Models.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJob
---@field ProcessingInputs? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingInputs List of input configurations for the processing job.
---@field ProcessingOutputConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingOutputConfig
---@field ProcessingJobName? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobName The name of the processing job.
---@field ProcessingResources? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingResources
---@field StoppingCondition? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingStoppingCondition
---@field AppSpecification? aws.sagemaker.AppSpecification
---@field Environment? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingEnvironmentMap Sets the environment variables in the Docker container.
---@field NetworkConfig? aws.sagemaker.NetworkConfig
---@field RoleArn? aws.sagemaker.RoleArn The ARN of the role used to create the processing job.
---@field ExperimentConfig? aws.sagemaker.ExperimentConfig
---@field ProcessingJobArn? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobArn The ARN of the processing job.
---@field ProcessingJobStatus? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobStatus The status of the processing job.
---@field ExitMessage? aws.sagemaker.ExitMessage A string, up to one KB in size, that contains metadata from the processing container when the processing job exits.
---@field FailureReason? aws.sagemaker.FailureReason A string, up to one KB in size, that contains the reason a processing job failed, if it failed.
---@field ProcessingEndTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp The time that the processing job ended.
---@field ProcessingStartTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp The time that the processing job started.
---@field LastModifiedTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp The time the processing job was last modified.
---@field CreationTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp The time the processing job was created.
---@field MonitoringScheduleArn? aws.sagemaker.MonitoringScheduleArn The ARN of a monitoring schedule for an endpoint associated with this processing job.
---@field AutoMLJobArn? aws.sagemaker.AutoMLJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the AutoML job associated with this processing job.
---@field TrainingJobArn? aws.sagemaker.TrainingJobArn The ARN of the training job associated with this processing job.
---@field Tags? aws.sagemaker.TagList An array of key-value pairs. For more information, see Using Cost Allocation Tags in the Amazon Web Services Billing and Cost Management User Guide.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobArn string

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobName string

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobStatus "InProgress"|"Completed"|"Failed"|"Stopping"|"Stopped"

---Metadata for a processing job step.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobStepMetadata
---@field Arn? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the processing job.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobSummaries aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobSummary[]

---Summary of information about a processing job.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobSummary
---@field ProcessingJobName aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobName The name of the processing job.
---@field ProcessingJobArn aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the processing job..
---@field CreationTime aws.sagemaker.Timestamp The time at which the processing job was created.
---@field ProcessingEndTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp The time at which the processing job completed.
---@field LastModifiedTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp A timestamp that indicates the last time the processing job was modified.
---@field ProcessingJobStatus aws.sagemaker.ProcessingJobStatus The status of the processing job.
---@field FailureReason? aws.sagemaker.FailureReason A string, up to one KB in size, that contains the reason a processing job failed, if it failed.
---@field ExitMessage? aws.sagemaker.ExitMessage An optional string, up to one KB in size, that contains metadata from the processing container when the processing job exits.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingLocalPath string

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingMaxRuntimeInSeconds number

---Describes the results of a processing job. The processing output must specify exactly one of either S3Output or FeatureStoreOutput types.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProcessingOutput
---@field OutputName aws.sagemaker.String The name for the processing job output.
---@field S3Output? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3Output Configuration for processing job outputs in Amazon S3.
---@field FeatureStoreOutput? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingFeatureStoreOutput Configuration for processing job outputs in Amazon SageMaker Feature Store. This processing output type is only supported when AppManaged is specified.
---@field AppManaged? aws.sagemaker.AppManaged When True, output operations such as data upload are managed natively by the processing job application. When False (default), output operations are managed by Amazon SageMaker.

---Configuration for uploading output from the processing container.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProcessingOutputConfig
---@field Outputs aws.sagemaker.ProcessingOutputs An array of outputs configuring the data to upload from the processing container.
---@field KmsKeyId? aws.sagemaker.KmsKeyId The Amazon Web Services Key Management Service (Amazon Web Services KMS) key that Amazon SageMaker uses to encrypt the processing job output. KmsKeyId can be an ID of a KMS key, ARN of a KMS key, or alias of a KMS key. The KmsKeyId is applied to all outputs.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingOutputs aws.sagemaker.ProcessingOutput[]

---Identifies the resources, ML compute instances, and ML storage volumes to deploy for a processing job. In distributed training, you specify more than one instance.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProcessingResources
---@field ClusterConfig aws.sagemaker.ProcessingClusterConfig The configuration for the resources in a cluster used to run the processing job.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3CompressionType "None"|"Gzip"

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3DataDistributionType "FullyReplicated"|"ShardedByS3Key"

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3DataType "ManifestFile"|"S3Prefix"

---Configuration for downloading input data from Amazon S3 into the processing container.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3Input
---@field S3Uri aws.sagemaker.S3Uri The URI of the Amazon S3 prefix Amazon SageMaker downloads data required to run a processing job.
---@field LocalPath? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingLocalPath The local path in your container where you want Amazon SageMaker to write input data to. LocalPath is an absolute path to the input data and must begin with /opt/ml/processing/. LocalPath is a required parameter when AppManaged is False (default).
---@field S3DataType aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3DataType|string Whether you use an S3Prefix or a ManifestFile for the data type. If you choose S3Prefix, S3Uri identifies a key name prefix. Amazon SageMaker uses all objects with the specified key name prefix for the processing job. If you choose ManifestFile, S3Uri identifies an object that is a manifest file containing a list of object keys that you want Amazon SageMaker to use for the processing job.
---@field S3InputMode? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3InputMode|string Whether to use File or Pipe input mode. In File mode, Amazon SageMaker copies the data from the input source onto the local ML storage volume before starting your processing container. This is the most commonly used input mode. In Pipe mode, Amazon SageMaker streams input data from the source directly to your processing container into named pipes without using the ML storage volume.
---@field S3DataDistributionType? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3DataDistributionType|string Whether to distribute the data from Amazon S3 to all processing instances with FullyReplicated, or whether the data from Amazon S3 is sharded by Amazon S3 key, downloading one shard of data to each processing instance.
---@field S3CompressionType? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3CompressionType|string Whether to GZIP-decompress the data in Amazon S3 as it is streamed into the processing container. Gzip can only be used when Pipe mode is specified as the S3InputMode. In Pipe mode, Amazon SageMaker streams input data from the source directly to your container without using the EBS volume.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3InputMode "Pipe"|"File"

---Configuration for uploading output data to Amazon S3 from the processing container.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3Output
---@field S3Uri aws.sagemaker.S3Uri A URI that identifies the Amazon S3 bucket where you want Amazon SageMaker to save the results of a processing job.
---@field LocalPath? aws.sagemaker.ProcessingLocalPath The local path of a directory where you want Amazon SageMaker to upload its contents to Amazon S3. LocalPath is an absolute path to a directory containing output files. This directory will be created by the platform and exist when your container's entrypoint is invoked.
---@field S3UploadMode aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3UploadMode|string Whether to upload the results of the processing job continuously or after the job completes.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingS3UploadMode "Continuous"|"EndOfJob"

---Configures conditions under which the processing job should be stopped, such as how long the processing job has been running. After the condition is met, the processing job is stopped.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProcessingStoppingCondition
---@field MaxRuntimeInSeconds aws.sagemaker.ProcessingMaxRuntimeInSeconds Specifies the maximum runtime in seconds.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProcessingVolumeSizeInGB number

---@alias aws.sagemaker.Processor "CPU"|"GPU"

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProductId string

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProductListings aws.sagemaker.String[]

---Identifies a model that you want to host and the resources chosen to deploy for hosting it. If you are deploying multiple models, tell SageMaker how to distribute traffic among the models by specifying variant weights. For more information on production variants, check Production variants.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariant
---@field VariantName aws.sagemaker.VariantName The name of the production variant.
---@field ModelName? aws.sagemaker.ModelName The name of the model that you want to host. This is the name that you specified when creating the model.
---@field InitialInstanceCount? aws.sagemaker.InitialTaskCount Number of instances to launch initially.
---@field InstanceType? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantInstanceType|string The ML compute instance type.
---@field InstancePools? aws.sagemaker.InstancePoolList A list of instance pools for the production variant. Each instance pool specifies an instance type and its priority for provisioning. Use instance pools to configure heterogeneous endpoints that deploy models across multiple instance types.
---@field VariantInstanceProvisionTimeoutInSeconds? aws.sagemaker.VariantInstanceProvisionTimeoutInSeconds The timeout value, in seconds, for provisioning instances for the production variant. When SageMaker encounters an insufficient capacity error while provisioning instances, it retries with the next instance pool (if configured) or waits until the timeout expires. This timeout applies only to capacity provisioning and does not include the time for model download or container startup.
---@field InitialVariantWeight? aws.sagemaker.VariantWeight Determines initial traffic distribution among all of the models that you specify in the endpoint configuration. The traffic to a production variant is determined by the ratio of the VariantWeight to the sum of all VariantWeight values across all ProductionVariants. If unspecified, it defaults to 1.0.
---@field AcceleratorType? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantAcceleratorType|string This parameter is no longer supported. Elastic Inference (EI) is no longer available.
---@field CoreDumpConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantCoreDumpConfig Specifies configuration for a core dump from the model container when the process crashes.
---@field ServerlessConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantServerlessConfig The serverless configuration for an endpoint. Specifies a serverless endpoint configuration instead of an instance-based endpoint configuration.
---@field VolumeSizeInGB? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantVolumeSizeInGB The size, in GB, of the ML storage volume attached to individual inference instance associated with the production variant. Currently only Amazon EBS gp2 storage volumes are supported.
---@field ModelDataDownloadTimeoutInSeconds? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantModelDataDownloadTimeoutInSeconds The timeout value, in seconds, to download and extract the model that you want to host from Amazon S3 to the individual inference instance associated with this production variant.
---@field ContainerStartupHealthCheckTimeoutInSeconds? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantContainerStartupHealthCheckTimeoutInSeconds The timeout value, in seconds, for your inference container to pass health check by SageMaker Hosting. For more information about health check, see How Your Container Should Respond to Health Check (Ping) Requests.
---@field EnableSSMAccess? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantSSMAccess You can use this parameter to turn on native Amazon Web Services Systems Manager (SSM) access for a production variant behind an endpoint. By default, SSM access is disabled for all production variants behind an endpoint. You can turn on or turn off SSM access for a production variant behind an existing endpoint by creating a new endpoint configuration and calling UpdateEndpoint.
---@field ManagedInstanceScaling? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantManagedInstanceScaling Settings that control the range in the number of instances that the endpoint provisions as it scales up or down to accommodate traffic.
---@field RoutingConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantRoutingConfig Settings that control how the endpoint routes incoming traffic to the instances that the endpoint hosts.
---@field InferenceAmiVersion? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantInferenceAmiVersion|string Specifies an option from a collection of preconfigured Amazon Machine Image (AMI) images. Each image is configured by Amazon Web Services with a set of software and driver versions. Amazon Web Services optimizes these configurations for different machine learning workloads.
---@field CapacityReservationConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantCapacityReservationConfig Settings for the capacity reservation for the compute instances that SageMaker AI reserves for an endpoint.
---@field AcceleratorPartitionLayouts? aws.sagemaker.AcceleratorPartitionLayouts The accelerator partition layout for the accelerators backing this production variant. A layout lists the partition profiles to carve on the accelerators it applies to; on NVIDIA GPUs these are Multi-Instance GPU (MIG) profiles such as mig-3g.40gb. Specify a single layout: SageMaker applies it uniformly to every accelerator on the variant's instance type, and you place one inference component on e...

