---Settings that control the range in the number of instances that the endpoint provisions as it scales up or down to accommodate traffic.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantManagedInstanceScaling
---@field Status? aws.sagemaker.ManagedInstanceScalingStatus|string Indicates whether managed instance scaling is enabled.
---@field MinInstanceCount? aws.sagemaker.ManagedInstanceScalingMinInstanceCount The minimum number of instances that the endpoint must retain when it scales down to accommodate a decrease in traffic.
---@field MaxInstanceCount? aws.sagemaker.ManagedInstanceScalingMaxInstanceCount The maximum number of instances that the endpoint can provision when it scales up to accommodate an increase in traffic.
---@field ScaleInPolicy? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantManagedInstanceScalingScaleInPolicy Configures the scale-in behavior for managed instance scaling.

---Configures the scale-in behavior for managed instance scaling.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantManagedInstanceScalingScaleInPolicy
---@field Strategy aws.sagemaker.ManagedInstanceScalingScaleInStrategy|string The strategy for scaling in instances.
---@field MaximumStepSize? aws.sagemaker.ManagedInstanceScalingMaximumStepSize The maximum number of instances that the endpoint can terminate at a time during a consolidation scale-in operation.
---@field CooldownInMinutes? aws.sagemaker.ManagedInstanceScalingCooldownInMinutes The cooldown period, in minutes, after the last endpoint operation before the endpoint evaluates consolidation scale-in opportunities.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantModelDataDownloadTimeoutInSeconds number

