---@class aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantStatus
---@field Status aws.sagemaker.VariantStatus The endpoint variant status which describes the current deployment stage status or operational status.
---@field StatusMessage? aws.sagemaker.VariantStatusMessage A message that describes the status of the production variant.
---@field StartTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp The start time of the current status change.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantStatusList aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantStatus[]

---Describes weight and capacities for a production variant associated with an endpoint. If you sent a request to the UpdateEndpointWeightsAndCapacities API and the endpoint status is Updating, you get different desired and current values.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantSummary
---@field VariantName aws.sagemaker.VariantName The name of the variant.
---@field DeployedImages? aws.sagemaker.DeployedImages An array of DeployedImage objects that specify the Amazon EC2 Container Registry paths of the inference images deployed on instances of this ProductionVariant.
---@field CurrentWeight? aws.sagemaker.VariantWeight The weight associated with the variant.
---@field DesiredWeight? aws.sagemaker.VariantWeight The requested weight, as specified in the UpdateEndpointWeightsAndCapacities request.
---@field CurrentInstanceCount? aws.sagemaker.TaskCount The number of instances associated with the variant.
---@field DesiredInstanceCount? aws.sagemaker.TaskCount The number of instances requested in the UpdateEndpointWeightsAndCapacities request.
---@field InstancePools? aws.sagemaker.InstancePoolSummaryList A list of instance pools for the production variant. Each pool indicates the instance type and the current number of instances of that type.
---@field VariantStatus? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantStatusList The endpoint variant status which describes the current deployment stage status or operational status.
---@field CurrentServerlessConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantServerlessConfig The serverless configuration for the endpoint.
---@field DesiredServerlessConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantServerlessConfig The serverless configuration requested for the endpoint update.
---@field ManagedInstanceScaling? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantManagedInstanceScaling Settings that control the range in the number of instances that the endpoint provisions as it scales up or down to accommodate traffic.
---@field RoutingConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantRoutingConfig Settings that control how the endpoint routes incoming traffic to the instances that the endpoint hosts.
---@field CapacityReservationConfig? aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantCapacityReservationSummary Settings for the capacity reservation for the compute instances that SageMaker AI reserves for an endpoint.
---@field AcceleratorPartitionLayouts? aws.sagemaker.AcceleratorPartitionLayouts The accelerator partition layout that SageMaker applies to this production variant. On NVIDIA GPUs, the profiles are Multi-Instance GPU (MIG) profiles. SageMaker returns the accelerator partition layout as you provided it when you created the variant, without normalization.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantSummaryList aws.sagemaker.ProductionVariantSummary[]

