---Container for the metadata for a Quality check step. For more information, see the topic on QualityCheck step in the Amazon SageMaker Developer Guide.
---@class aws.sagemaker.QualityCheckStepMetadata
---@field CheckType? aws.sagemaker.String256 The type of the Quality check step.
---@field BaselineUsedForDriftCheckStatistics? aws.sagemaker.String1024 The Amazon S3 URI of the baseline statistics file used for the drift check.
---@field BaselineUsedForDriftCheckConstraints? aws.sagemaker.String1024 The Amazon S3 URI of the baseline constraints file used for the drift check.
---@field CalculatedBaselineStatistics? aws.sagemaker.String1024 The Amazon S3 URI of the newly calculated baseline statistics file.
---@field CalculatedBaselineConstraints? aws.sagemaker.String1024 The Amazon S3 URI of the newly calculated baseline constraints file.
---@field ModelPackageGroupName? aws.sagemaker.String256 The model package group name.
---@field ViolationReport? aws.sagemaker.String1024 The Amazon S3 URI of violation report if violations are detected.
---@field CheckJobArn? aws.sagemaker.String256 The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Quality check processing job that was run by this step execution.
---@field SkipCheck? aws.sagemaker.Boolean This flag indicates if the drift check against the previous baseline will be skipped or not. If it is set to False, the previous baseline of the configured check type must be available.
---@field RegisterNewBaseline? aws.sagemaker.Boolean This flag indicates if a newly calculated baseline can be accessed through step properties BaselineUsedForDriftCheckConstraints and BaselineUsedForDriftCheckStatistics. If it is set to False, the previous baseline of the configured check type must also be available. These can be accessed through the BaselineUsedForDriftCheckConstraints and BaselineUsedForDriftCheckStatistics properties.

---A set of filters to narrow the set of lineage entities connected to the StartArn(s) returned by the QueryLineage API action.
---@class aws.sagemaker.QueryFilters
---@field Types? aws.sagemaker.QueryTypes Filter the lineage entities connected to the StartArn by type. For example: DataSet, Model, Endpoint, or ModelDeployment.
---@field LineageTypes? aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageTypes Filter the lineage entities connected to the StartArn(s) by the type of the lineage entity.
---@field CreatedBefore? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp Filter the lineage entities connected to the StartArn(s) by created date.
---@field CreatedAfter? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp Filter the lineage entities connected to the StartArn(s) after the create date.
---@field ModifiedBefore? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp Filter the lineage entities connected to the StartArn(s) before the last modified date.
---@field ModifiedAfter? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp Filter the lineage entities connected to the StartArn(s) after the last modified date.
---@field Properties? aws.sagemaker.QueryProperties Filter the lineage entities connected to the StartArn(s) by a set if property key value pairs. If multiple pairs are provided, an entity is included in the results if it matches any of the provided pairs.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageMaxDepth number

---@alias aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageMaxResults number

---@class aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageRequest
---@field StartArns? aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageStartArns A list of resource Amazon Resource Name (ARN) that represent the starting point for your lineage query.
---@field Direction? aws.sagemaker.Direction|string Associations between lineage entities have a direction. This parameter determines the direction from the StartArn(s) that the query traverses.
---@field IncludeEdges? aws.sagemaker.Boolean Setting this value to True retrieves not only the entities of interest but also the Associations and lineage entities on the path. Set to False to only return lineage entities that match your query.
---@field Filters? aws.sagemaker.QueryFilters A set of filtering parameters that allow you to specify which entities should be returned.
---@field MaxDepth? aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageMaxDepth The maximum depth in lineage relationships from the StartArns that are traversed. Depth is a measure of the number of Associations from the StartArn entity to the matched results.
---@field MaxResults? aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageMaxResults Limits the number of vertices in the results. Use the NextToken in a response to to retrieve the next page of results.
---@field NextToken? aws.sagemaker.String8192 Limits the number of vertices in the request. Use the NextToken in a response to to retrieve the next page of results.

---@class aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageResponse
---@field Vertices? aws.sagemaker.Vertices A list of vertices connected to the start entity(ies) in the lineage graph.
---@field Edges? aws.sagemaker.Edges A list of edges that connect vertices in the response.
---@field NextToken? aws.sagemaker.String8192 Limits the number of vertices in the response. Use the NextToken in a response to to retrieve the next page of results.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageStartArns aws.sagemaker.AssociationEntityArn[]

---@alias aws.sagemaker.QueryLineageTypes (aws.sagemaker.LineageType|string)[]

---@alias aws.sagemaker.QueryProperties { [string]: aws.sagemaker.String256 }

---@alias aws.sagemaker.QueryTypes aws.sagemaker.String40[]

