---Describes the resources, including machine learning (ML) compute instances and ML storage volumes, to use for model training.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ResourceConfig
---@field InstanceType? aws.sagemaker.TrainingInstanceType|string The ML compute instance type.
---@field InstanceCount? aws.sagemaker.TrainingInstanceCount The number of ML compute instances to use. For distributed training, provide a value greater than 1.
---@field VolumeSizeInGB? aws.sagemaker.OptionalVolumeSizeInGB The size of the ML storage volume that you want to provision.
---@field VolumeKmsKeyId? aws.sagemaker.KmsKeyId The Amazon Web Services KMS key that SageMaker uses to encrypt data on the storage volume attached to the ML compute instance(s) that run the training job.
---@field KeepAlivePeriodInSeconds? aws.sagemaker.KeepAlivePeriodInSeconds The duration of time in seconds to retain configured resources in a warm pool for subsequent training jobs.
---@field InstanceGroups? aws.sagemaker.InstanceGroups The configuration of a heterogeneous cluster in JSON format.
---@field TrainingPlanArn? aws.sagemaker.TrainingPlanArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN); of the training plan to use for this resource configuration.
---@field InstancePlacementConfig? aws.sagemaker.InstancePlacementConfig Configuration for how training job instances are placed and allocated within UltraServers. Only applicable for UltraServer capacity.
---@field InstancePreferences? aws.sagemaker.InstancePreferenceList An ordered list of ML compute instance types for the training job, in priority order. SageMaker launches the training job on the first instance type in the list that has available capacity. If capacity is insufficient, SageMaker evaluates the next instance type in the preferred list. Exactly one instance type is selected for the job.
---@field SelectedInstanceType? aws.sagemaker.TrainingInstanceType|string The instance type that SageMaker selected for the job from the provided InstancePreferences. The job is billed for this instance type and count. Returned by DescribeTrainingJob after an instance type is selected. This field is read-only and isn't accepted in CreateTrainingJob requests.
---@field SelectedInstanceCount? aws.sagemaker.TrainingInstanceCount The number of instances of SelectedInstanceType that the training job launched with. The job is billed for this instance type and count. Returned by DescribeTrainingJob after an instance type is selected. This field is read-only and isn't accepted in CreateTrainingJob requests.

---The ResourceConfig to update KeepAlivePeriodInSeconds. Other fields in the ResourceConfig cannot be updated.
---@class aws.sagemaker.ResourceConfigForUpdate
---@field KeepAlivePeriodInSeconds aws.sagemaker.KeepAlivePeriodInSeconds The KeepAlivePeriodInSeconds value specified in the ResourceConfig to update.

