---@class aws.sagemaker.SearchRequest
---@field Resource aws.sagemaker.ResourceType|string The name of the SageMaker resource to search for.
---@field SearchExpression? aws.sagemaker.SearchExpression A Boolean conditional statement. Resources must satisfy this condition to be included in search results. You must provide at least one subexpression, filter, or nested filter. The maximum number of recursive SubExpressions, NestedFilters, and Filters that can be included in a SearchExpression object is 50.
---@field SortBy? aws.sagemaker.ResourcePropertyName The name of the resource property used to sort the SearchResults. The default is LastModifiedTime.
---@field SortOrder? aws.sagemaker.SearchSortOrder|string How SearchResults are ordered. Valid values are Ascending or Descending. The default is Descending.
---@field NextToken? aws.sagemaker.NextToken If more than MaxResults resources match the specified SearchExpression, the response includes a NextToken. The NextToken can be passed to the next SearchRequest to continue retrieving results.
---@field MaxResults? aws.sagemaker.MaxResults The maximum number of results to return.
---@field CrossAccountFilterOption? aws.sagemaker.CrossAccountFilterOption|string A cross account filter option. When the value is "CrossAccount" the search results will only include resources made discoverable to you from other accounts. When the value is "SameAccount" or null the search results will only include resources from your account. Default is null. For more information on searching for resources made discoverable to your account, see Search discoverable resources in ...
---@field VisibilityConditions? aws.sagemaker.VisibilityConditionsList Limits the results of your search request to the resources that you can access.

---@class aws.sagemaker.SearchResponse
---@field Results aws.sagemaker.SearchResultsList A list of SearchRecord objects.
---@field NextToken? aws.sagemaker.NextToken If the result of the previous Search request was truncated, the response includes a NextToken. To retrieve the next set of results, use the token in the next request.
---@field TotalHits? aws.sagemaker.TotalHits The total number of matching results.

---@alias aws.sagemaker.SearchResultsList aws.sagemaker.SearchRecord[]

---@alias aws.sagemaker.SearchSortOrder "Ascending"|"Descending"

---@class aws.sagemaker.SearchTrainingPlanOfferingsRequest
---@field InstanceType? aws.sagemaker.ReservedCapacityInstanceType|string The type of instance you want to search for in the available training plan offerings. This field allows you to filter the search results based on the specific compute resources you require for your SageMaker training jobs or SageMaker HyperPod clusters. When searching for training plan offerings, specifying the instance type helps you find Reserved Instances that match your computational needs.
---@field InstanceCount? aws.sagemaker.ReservedCapacityInstanceCount The number of instances you want to reserve in the training plan offerings. This allows you to specify the quantity of compute resources needed for your SageMaker training jobs or SageMaker HyperPod clusters, helping you find reserved capacity offerings that match your requirements.
---@field UltraServerType? aws.sagemaker.UltraServerType The type of UltraServer to search for, such as ml.u-p6e-gb200x72.
---@field UltraServerCount? aws.sagemaker.UltraServerCount The number of UltraServers to search for.
---@field StartTimeAfter? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp A filter to search for training plan offerings with a start time after a specified date.
---@field EndTimeBefore? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp A filter to search for reserved capacity offerings with an end time before a specified date.
---@field DurationHours? aws.sagemaker.TrainingPlanDurationHoursInput The desired duration in hours for the training plan offerings.
---@field TargetResources? aws.sagemaker.SageMakerResourceNames The target resources (e.g., SageMaker Training Jobs, SageMaker HyperPod, SageMaker Endpoints, Studio apps) to search for in the offerings.
---@field TrainingPlanArn? aws.sagemaker.String The Amazon Resource Name (ARN); of an existing training plan to search for extension offerings. When specified, the API returns extension offerings that can be used to extend the specified training plan.

---@class aws.sagemaker.SearchTrainingPlanOfferingsResponse
