---A batch transform job. For information about SageMaker batch transform, see Use Batch Transform.
---@class aws.sagemaker.TransformJob
---@field TransformJobName? aws.sagemaker.TransformJobName The name of the transform job.
---@field TransformJobArn? aws.sagemaker.TransformJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the transform job.
---@field TransformJobStatus? aws.sagemaker.TransformJobStatus The status of the transform job.
---@field FailureReason? aws.sagemaker.FailureReason If the transform job failed, the reason it failed.
---@field ModelName? aws.sagemaker.ModelName The name of the model associated with the transform job.
---@field MaxConcurrentTransforms? aws.sagemaker.MaxConcurrentTransforms The maximum number of parallel requests that can be sent to each instance in a transform job. If MaxConcurrentTransforms is set to 0 or left unset, SageMaker checks the optional execution-parameters to determine the settings for your chosen algorithm. If the execution-parameters endpoint is not enabled, the default value is 1. For built-in algorithms, you don't need to set a value for MaxConcurren...
---@field ModelClientConfig? aws.sagemaker.ModelClientConfig
---@field MaxPayloadInMB? aws.sagemaker.MaxPayloadInMB The maximum allowed size of the payload, in MB. A payload is the data portion of a record (without metadata). The value in MaxPayloadInMB must be greater than, or equal to, the size of a single record. To estimate the size of a record in MB, divide the size of your dataset by the number of records. To ensure that the records fit within the maximum payload size, we recommend using a slightly larger...
---@field BatchStrategy? aws.sagemaker.BatchStrategy Specifies the number of records to include in a mini-batch for an HTTP inference request. A record is a single unit of input data that inference can be made on. For example, a single line in a CSV file is a record.
---@field Environment? aws.sagemaker.TransformEnvironmentMap The environment variables to set in the Docker container. We support up to 16 key and values entries in the map.
---@field TransformInput? aws.sagemaker.TransformInput
---@field TransformOutput? aws.sagemaker.TransformOutput
---@field DataCaptureConfig? aws.sagemaker.BatchDataCaptureConfig
---@field TransformResources? aws.sagemaker.TransformResources
---@field CreationTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp A timestamp that shows when the transform Job was created.
---@field TransformStartTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp Indicates when the transform job starts on ML instances. You are billed for the time interval between this time and the value of TransformEndTime.
---@field TransformEndTime? aws.sagemaker.Timestamp Indicates when the transform job has been completed, or has stopped or failed. You are billed for the time interval between this time and the value of TransformStartTime.
---@field LabelingJobArn? aws.sagemaker.LabelingJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the labeling job that created the transform job.
---@field AutoMLJobArn? aws.sagemaker.AutoMLJobArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the AutoML job that created the transform job.
---@field DataProcessing? aws.sagemaker.DataProcessing
